<title>USA: USDA donates wheat to Georgia and Armenia.</title>
<headline>USDA donates wheat to Georgia and Armenia.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Department said Thursday it would donate about 6,500 tonnes of wheat to Armenia and Georgia.</p>
<p>USDA said it will donate the wheat to Cooperative for Assistance and Relief Everywhere (CARE) which will sell the grain through a sealed-bid public auction to private sector traders. CARE will use the proceeds to support agricultural development projects in the two countries.</p>
<p>The donations will be made through USDA's Food for Progress program. The supply period for both is fiscal year 1997.</p>
